  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Opioid use disorder on buprenorphine (F11.20)</content>. Stable on 16 mg with no opioid use; urine test shows buprenorphine only. The four-week gap since the one-week visit was longer than advised early in treatment, but weekly counseling calls continued and no harm resulted. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. [S]<list><item>Continue buprenorphine with naloxone 16 mg daily.</item><item>Video check-ins every two weeks between visits while she tours.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder on acamprosate (F10.20)</content>. PEth down from 312 to 96 ng/mL: drinking reduced, not stopped. AST 38, ALT 30, GGT 52 U/L, all improving. PHQ-9 7. [S]<list><item>Continue acamprosate; take the midday dose with lunch, with a phone reminder.</item><item>Her goal for now is no more than two drinks on performance nights and none on other days.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Buprenorphine dose, adherence, cravings, withdrawal, and side effects</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>16 mg daily without gaps; brief cravings; no sedation</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Visit frequency</td><td>Every 1 to 2 weeks in the first month after starting, then every 2 to 4 weeks until stable</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Four weeks since the one-week visit, longer than the one to two weeks advised in the first month, because she was on tour; the planned call-in visit at two weeks did not happen. Weekly counseling calls continued, and no harm resulted. Corrective action: video check-ins every two weeks between visits while touring</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Urine drug testing, including fentanyl, explained as part of care rather than as a test of trust</td><td>At the start, then about monthly early in treatment and as needed</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Buprenorphine and norbuprenorphine only</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Prescription drug monitoring program check</td><td>Before each buprenorphine prescription</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No other prescriptions</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Naloxone at home and in her bag, and a trained companion</td><td>At the start; check and replace at each visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>In her bag and at home; not used</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Overdose prevention: never using alone and fentanyl test strips</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Counseling and peer recovery support</td><td>Offered to everyone; not a condition of medication</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Weekly counseling by phone on tour; peer coach by phone</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Drinking and PEth</td><td>PEth at intake and at each check while drinking continues; AUDIT-C yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PEth 96 ng/mL, from 312; two or three drinks on performance nights</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Acamprosate adherence and kidney function</td><td>Kidney function before starting; adherence every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Missing some midday doses; reminder set</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Thiamine</td><td>While drinking heavily</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taking thiamine daily</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Liver tests (AST, ALT, GGT, albumin, bilirubin)</td><td>At intake, then every 1 to 3 months while drinking is heavy, and yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AST 38, ALT 30, GGT 52 U/L, improving</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>FIB-4 fibrosis score</td><td>At intake; repeat in 6 to 12 months with ongoing drinking, and every 1 to 2 years</td><td>Up to date</td><td>1.18 at intake; repeat at six months</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Vibration-controlled transient elastography</td><td>If FIB-4 is 1.3 or higher</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>FIB-4 below 1.3</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Hepatitis A and B vaccines</td><td>Hepatitis B two doses 4 weeks apart; hepatitis A two doses 6 months apart</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Hepatitis B dose 2 given today; hepatitis A dose 2 at six months</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression screen (PHQ-9)</td><td>At intake and at each recovery visit while symptoms are present</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 7, item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide and overdose risk review, safety plan, and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No thoughts of suicide or self-harm; safety plan and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline in her phone</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Stay on buprenorphine without interruption through six months, including through any return to use. In progress; target 1948-10-19 [S]</item><item>Naloxone at home and in her bag, and a friend trained to use it, by the one-week visit. Outcome by 1948-04-27: Two naloxone two-packs dispensed; her friend trained [S]</item><item>Reduce drinking to PEth below 20 ng/mL, or to the level she chooses, by six months. In progress; target 1948-10-19 [S]</item><item>Hepatitis A and B vaccine series completed by six months. In progress; target 1948-10-19 [S]</item><item>PHQ-9 score below 5 by six months. In progress; target 1948-10-19 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), dose 2 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: The ASAM National Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Opioid Use Disorder: 2020 Focused Update (2020); Treatment Options for Substance Use Disorder (medications for opioid and alcohol use disorders) (2026); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); Diagnosis and Treatment of Alcohol-Associated Liver Diseases: 2019 Practice Guidance From the American Association for the Study of Liver Diseases (2019); AASLD Practice Guideline on blood-based noninvasive liver disease assessment of hepatic fibrosis and steatosis (2025); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Video check-ins every two weeks while touring. Three-month visit with PEth, liver tests, and the PHQ-9. Next scheduled visit 1948-07-20: three-month review after a return to opioid use: adjusting the recovery plan. [S]</paragraph></text>

